# Zustand State Management Patterns

## Store Structure

```javascript
import { create } from "zustand";
import { STATUS } from "@/constants/db";

const useAuthStore = create((set, get) => ({
  // State properties
  user: null,
  userFetchStatus: STATUS.LOADING,

  // Synchronous actions
  setUser: (user) => set(() => ({ user })),
  setUserFetchStatus: (status) => set(() => ({ userFetchStatus: status })),

  // Async actions with error handling
  loadUser: async () => {
    if (get().user) return; // Prevent unnecessary calls
    const response = await getUserSession();
    if (response.error || !response.data.session) {
      set(() => ({ user: null }));
    } else {
      set(() => ({ user: response.data.session.user }));
    }
    set(() => ({ userFetchStatus: STATUS.FETCHED }));
  },
}));
```

## Component Integration

```javascript
// Use useShallow for multiple selections to prevent unnecessary re-renders
import { useShallow } from "zustand/react/shallow";

const { tasks, setTasks, updateTaskInStore } = useTasksStore(
  useShallow((state) => ({
    tasks: state.tasks,
    setTasks: state.setTasks,
    updateTaskInStore: state.updateTask,
  }))
);
```

## Store Actions Patterns

```javascript
// Optimistic updates
const updateTask = (updatedTask) => {
  set((state) => ({
    tasks: state.tasks.map((task) =>
      task.id === updatedTask.id ? updatedTask : task
    ),
  }));
};

// Array operations
const setTasks = (tasks) => set(() => ({ tasks }));
const addTask = (newTask) =>
  set((state) => ({
    tasks: [...state.tasks, newTask],
  }));
```

## Best Practices

- Use status constants for loading states (`STATUS.LOADING`, `STATUS.FETCHED`)
- Implement optimistic updates where appropriate
- Check existing state before API calls (`if (get().user) return`)
- Use descriptive action names that indicate what they do
- Keep stores focused on single domains (auth, tasks, journals)
- Use get() function to access current state within actions
- Return meaningful data from async actions

## Loading State Management

```javascript
// Use consistent loading state patterns
const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);

const loadData = async () => {
  setIsLoading(true);
  try {
    const data = await fetchData();
    setData(data);
  } finally {
    setIsLoading(false);
  }
};
```

